window.STUDY={"id":"ap-24-instrument-dial","code":"AP-24","title":"Instrument dial · 24 h in stipple","fig":"4.24","kicker":"Application · 24","lede":"A day of readings wound onto a clock face: 48 half-hour bins radiate from a hairline ring, midnight at the top.","body":["Each bin is a count of dots, and its tip runs out instead of stopping at a hard cap. The current bin and the needle print in ember, the readout beside them in the same ink, and the hours are struck in type."],"source":"Made with the effect set: Stipple ramp, Roller run-out, Typewriter strike, Paper tooth.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":844},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are dials of the effects: open Parameters and pick an effect.","paramsHint":"Every dial of the effects this piece uses.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"u-meter","job":"screen","title":"Instrument dial · 24 h in stipple","aspect":"16/9","uses":["fx-01-stipple","fx-02-ink-edge","fx-07-typewriter","fx-03-paper-tooth"]},"reference":{"grammar":"A day of readings wound onto a clock face: 48 half-hour bins radiate from a hairline ring, midnight at the top. Each bin is a count of dots, and its tip runs out instead of stopping at a hard cap. The current bin and the needle print in ember, the readout beside them in the same ink, and the hours are struck in type."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-01-stipple","name":"Stipple ramp","short":"FX-01","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"pitch":{"value":1.4,"range":[0.8,16],"label":"Pitch","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"distance between dot sites. It sets the COUNT of dots, not their size"},"dotR":{"value":0.5,"range":[0.2,4],"label":"Dot radius","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"radius of a full-value dot, independent of pitch"},"screen":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Screen · FM ↔ AM","step":0.01,"note":"0 = value changes how many dots print; 1 = how big they are"},"sAngle":{"value":0,"range":[0,90],"label":"Screen angle","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"rotates the dot lattice. 45° is the classic single-ink angle: the eye reads the rows least, and they never beat against the pixel grid"},"jitter":{"value":0.85,"range":[0,1],"label":"Jitter","step":0.01,"note":"site offset inside its cell (0 = lattice)"},"sizeVar":{"value":0.1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Size variance","step":0.01,"note":"per-dot radius spread"},"irregular":{"value":0.06,"range":[0,1],"label":"Nib irregularity","step":0.01,"note":"vertex wobble of each footprint: a nib, not a disc"},"pressure":{"value":1,"range":[0.3,1],"label":"Pen pressure","step":0.01,"note":"film per dot and how many valleys it skips (with Starve)"},"angle":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ramp angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction of the linear ramp"},"from":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,1],"label":"From","step":0.01,"note":"value at the start of the field"},"to":{"value":1,"range":[0,1],"label":"To","step":0.01,"note":"value at the end of the field"},"fScale":{"value":140,"range":[20,500],"label":"Field scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"noise field wavelength"},"rag":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,1.5],"label":"Edge rag","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"how far the stock's tooth pushes each dot edge in and out. 0 = perfect discs"},"starve":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"valleys inside a dot that the nib skips. The pinholes follow the stock height, AA-edged, and grow as pressure drops"},"wick":{"value":0.08,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried a short way out along fibers"},"mottle":{"value":0.1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation varying the film"},"aL":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink A · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"aC":{"value":0.004,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink A · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ah":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink A · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"bL":{"value":0.64,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink B · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"bC":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink B · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"bh":{"value":38,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink B · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.25,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure; with the film rule, thicker = deeper and more saturated (Beer–Lambert)"},"mInset":{"value":14,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":4,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":70,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":10,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"mBite":{"value":0.15,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":5,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Site lattice at the pitch (CSS px), jittered. Value field (linear · radial · noise) eased from → to. Screen: FM keeps a site when its blue-noise rank < value; AM keeps every site with radius ∝ √value; the dial interpolates. The mask is sampled at the site, so dots are whole or absent. Each dot is geometry: a signed distance to an irregular nib outline (7 vertex radii), so its edge is always 1 device px of anti-aliasing, never a blur. The stock edits the edge: the distance is displaced by the stock height (edge rag), valleys inside the dot can starve, fibers wick a short way out. Film τ = thickness × pressure. Color: Beer–Lambert film in linear light (or a coverage mix). Ink B overprints by the same film product. Light last: × the stock's shading under the sheet light.","limits":"pitch < 1.2 px: sites merge into flat tone at 1×: the stipple stops reading as marks. dot radius < .3 px: below ~½ device px at 1× a dot is a gray pixel, not a mark. dot radius > ½ pitch: dots fuse into a solid; FM loses its range. edge rag > .9 px: dots read as fuzz, not ink. selection white: clumps and voids at low density"},{"id":"fx-02-ink-edge","name":"Roller run-out","short":"FX-02","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"streak":{"value":1.25,"range":[1,10],"label":"Streak","step":0.1,"note":"film-split clumps stretched along the stroke: a dry roller, a dragged brush"},"pressure":{"value":1,"range":[0.4,1],"label":"Roller pressure","step":0.01,"note":"pressure in the solid; below 1 the body starts to open up"},"angle":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Stroke angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction the roller travels (it runs out along this vector)"},"edge":{"value":1.7,"range":[0,1.7],"label":"Edge position","step":0.005,"note":"where the run-out is centered across the plate"},"width":{"value":4,"range":[1,420],"label":"Transition","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"width of the run-out band"},"wAmp":{"value":18,"range":[0,90],"label":"Edge warp","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far the edge line wanders"},"wScale":{"value":90,"range":[8,400],"label":"Warp scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander"},"wOct":{"value":3,"range":[1,5],"label":"Warp octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"detail in the wander"},"bite":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0.004,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0.05,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.18,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0.005,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.3,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert: thicker = deeper, more saturated)"},"mInset":{"value":14,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":60,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":14,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"mBite":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":9,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Pressure = dropoff curve of the signed distance to a warped edge line (stroke direction, transition width), × the mask. Ink chain: the stock height under the inked area (blended with film-splitting noise, clumped and streaked along the stroke) is ranked to percentiles; pressure P inks exactly the top P of the surface, peaks first. Starve: valleys below the threshold never take ink. Wick: fibers carry ink past the edge. Mottle: paper formation thins the film. Film thickness thins with pressure unless the film breaks up; color = Beer–Lambert film in linear light. Light last: × the stock's shading. The ink sits in the tooth, not on top of it.","limits":"transition < 4 px: reads as a hard vector edge: no run-out to see. break-up < .3: the edge becomes a gradient: the \"AI gradient\" failure. stock bite < .3: speckle stops following the paper and reads as digital dither. streak > 6: marks read as scanlines unless the angle is off-axis"},{"id":"fx-07-typewriter","name":"Typewriter strike","short":"FX-07","atoms":["transfer","deform"],"params":{"fsize":{"value":34,"range":[8,48],"label":"Size","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"type size in CSS px; bold below 15 px"},"lead":{"value":1.5,"range":[1,2.4],"label":"Leading","step":0.01,"note":"line spacing as a multiple of the size"},"vari":{"value":0.15,"range":[0,1],"label":"Key variance","step":0.01,"note":"how unevenly keys strike"},"half":{"value":0.05,"range":[0,0.4],"label":"Half strikes","step":0.005,"note":"share of glyphs where only the top or bottom lands"},"jx":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,2],"label":"Jitter x","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"horizontal offset per strike"},"jy":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,2],"label":"Jitter y","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"vertical offset per strike"},"rot":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,4],"label":"Rotation","step":0.05,"unit":"°","note":"rotation spread per strike"},"exhaust":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ribbon wear","step":0.01,"note":"ink fading along the text"},"ribbon":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ribbon texture","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ribbon weave shows in the glyphs"},"rcount":{"value":95,"range":[20,200],"label":"Ribbon count","step":1,"unit":"/100px","note":"ribbon threads per 100 CSS px"},"squash":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink squash","step":0.01,"note":"film pooling at the glyph edge"},"impress":{"value":0.15,"range":[0,1],"label":"Press depth","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"how deep each strike dents the stock"},"diffuse":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"bite":{"value":0.55,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":0.85,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.12,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":0.8,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0.006,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.15,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert)"},"seed":{"value":7,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Text in Courier Prime (a typewriter slab; bold below 15 px, as a light strike loses thin strokes), one strike per glyph on the main thread: pressure = ribbon life (exhausting along the page) × key variance; offset, rotation, an occasional dropped baseline; a half strike is a linear pressure ramp across the glyph, fading top or bottom. Ribbon: a plain weave at the ribbon count. Ink transfers through thread crossings, less through the gaps. Ink chain: pressure × ribbon vs stock-height percentile; ink squash pools film at the glyph edge. Impression: the strike dents the stock (blurred glyph × pressure); light from the combined height. Color: Beer–Lambert film.","limits":"ribbon count < 30 /100 px: weave reads as a screen pattern on the type. jitter > 1.5 px: reads as broken font rendering. size < 7 px: strokes thinner than the tooth lose the ribbon texture"},{"id":"fx-03-paper-tooth","name":"Paper tooth","short":"FX-03","atoms":["form"],"params":{"scale":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,24],"label":"Tooth scale","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"feature size of the tooth (noise wavelength), not a tile zoom"},"oct":{"value":3,"range":[1,6],"label":"Octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"layers of finer detail"},"fibers":{"value":1.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Fibers","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"laid fibers per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"fLen":{"value":14,"range":[2,80],"label":"Fiber length","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber length"},"fWidth":{"value":0.4,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Fiber width","step":0.02,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber width"},"pits":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,40],"label":"Pits","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"depressions per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"pers":{"value":0.42,"range":[0.15,0.85],"label":"Persistence","step":0.01,"note":"amplitude kept per octave: the spectral dropoff of the tooth"},"aniso":{"value":1.5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Anisotropy","step":0.05,"note":"tooth stretched along the grain angle. Machine-made paper is never isotropic; 1 = the 1999 \"paper\" filter look"},"form":{"value":0.1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Formation","step":0.01,"note":"low-frequency cloudiness of the sheet (fiber flocs); also mottles any ink printed on it"},"formScale":{"value":60,"range":[10,200],"label":"Formation scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"size of the flocs"},"fAngle":{"value":6,"range":[0,180],"label":"Grain angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"machine direction of the fibers and the tooth"},"fSpread":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Grain spread","step":0.01,"note":"0 = all fibers on the grain; 1 = any direction"},"depth":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Relief","step":0.005,"unit":"px","note":"height of the tooth in CSS px: how hard the light can rake it. The slider is weighted to the subtle end."},"diffuse":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"fRaise":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fiber raise","step":0.01,"note":"how far fibers stand proud of the sheet"},"pDepth":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pit depth","step":0.01,"note":"how deep pits go"},"paperL":{"value":0.968,"range":[0.85,1],"label":"Paper L","step":0.001,"note":"OKLab lightness of the stock under the sheet light. Below 1 so lit walls, foil and sheen have headroom to brighten; 1 = the white of the page (highlights clip)"},"fDark":{"value":0.014,"range":[0,0.15],"label":"Fiber tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening of fibers"},"pDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Pit tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening in pits"},"tL":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"tC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Fill tint · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"th":{"value":250,"range":[0,360],"label":"Fill tint · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"tAmt":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint amount","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ambient fill takes the tint (shadows go cool / warm)"},"mInset":{"value":22,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":28,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"lift":{"value":1,"range":[0,4],"label":"Sheet lift","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"thickness / curl of the sheet: sizes its shadow on the page"},"mBite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":21,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Height = fbm at the tooth scale (octaves, persistence = how fast detail drops off), reshaped by the distribution curve; blended with low-frequency formation. Fibers: curved capsules at a count per 100 × 100 CSS px near the grain angle, raised into the height; pits: small depressions. Both also darken the albedo slightly. Normal from the height gradient → Lambert under the sheet light (azimuth + elevation from the light puck). Diffuse share vs ambient fill; the fill can be tinted. The same field is the stock for FX-01 and FX-02: its peaks take ink first, its valleys starve, its fibers wick. Mask = the sheet's cut or deckle edge; the sheet casts a contact + ambient shadow onto the page by the same light.","limits":"relief > .6 px: reads as stucco: the stock-filter emboss look. anisotropy < 1.3: isotropic tooth reads as a 1999 paper filter. tooth scale < .8 px: collapses into per-pixel noise: digital grain. fibers > 30 /100×100 px: felt, not paper. light elevation < 15°: every fiber becomes a hard ridge; ok for a raking-light study, not for a page"}],"pass_order":["Stipple ramp · Tone made of whole pen dots.","Roller run-out · A solid that runs out.","Typewriter strike · Each glyph is a separate strike: its own pressure, a slight offset and rotation, sometimes only half the face lands.","Paper tooth · White stock that is not a screen."]}};
